From 09332ffebeb20f9a6899b0251881270b1228be85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 02:43:18 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 perf-0: page timing, presentation feedback,
 histograms and processes for the host

perf-0 measures ReArc against its budgets (docs/PERFORMANCE-PLAN.md). The
host needs the engine's own clocks for page loads and content presentation,
so ABI 1.44 (perf_metrics, bridge 0.46.0) adds four measurement-only
channels; with no callback set nothing is attached and behavior is
unchanged. ReArcEngineSetPageTimingCallback attaches page_load_metrics
(MetricsWebContentsObserver with Chromium's UmaPageLoadMetricsObserver, so
PageLoad.PaintTiming.* match Chrome) to tabs created afterwards and reports
response start, first paint, FCP, DCL, load and each LCP candidate.
ReArcEngineSetViewPresentationCallback reports a lease's hidden-to-visible
transition with Chromium's Browser.Tabs.TotalSwitchDuration3 measurement
(WebContents::SetTabSwitchStartTime before VISIBLE) and, after a
ResizeView, the first renderer frame activated at the new pixel size and the
browser compositor's next presented frame. ReArcMetricsGetHistogram returns
a UMA histogram after merging child deltas; ReArcEngineGetProcesses lists
the browser, renderers (profile, extension, hosted tabs) and child
processes with phys_footprint, resident size and CPU time. Times are
microseconds on mach_absolute_time's clock. rearc_perf.{h,cc} adds
os_signpost intervals under net.rearc.engine (abi: hot entry points and
every event/completion dispatch; profile: ProfileOpen; view:
TabSwitchPresentation, ResizeToPresentation; tab: page milestones).
framework.exports and framework.order list the four new functions.
Existing ABI layouts remain unchanged.

Last rebased: 2026-11-05 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
